                <pb facs="0107" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg33"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Royal decree of</hi> 19<hi rendition="#italic">th
                        May,</hi> 1866, <hi rendition="#italic">relative to capture and confiscation
                        of merchant vessels of enemies</hi>.</head>
                <p>On the propositions of the minister of state I declare that, in event of war,
                    merchant vessels belonging to subjects of hostile states shall not be subjected
                    to capture and confiscation by my ships of war so long as reciprocity be
                    practiced by the hostile states.</p>
                <p>The preceding decree has no application to such vessels as would be subject to
                    capture and confiscation, even if they were neutral ships.</p>
                <p>Let this, my decree, be published in the Law Register.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILHELM.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 19, 1866</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
